From 6d13d5341e53719ca993fc34e93f5b374940339f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-rg35xx <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] owlfb: RG35XX framebuffer layout and flip path recovered
 from the vendor kernel

Matches the running RG35XX kernel (function-level diff of its Image):
- owlfb_info holds 2 overlays (OWLFB_MAX_OVL_PER_FB 2); owlfb_device gains
  the DT "rotate" and "mode" values; DT values are read as u32 (the public
  source passed u16 locals to of_property_read_u32), plus "bpp".
- fb memory sized from the panel: fb0 = 5 double-buffered screens, other
  fbs one; overlay reserve 512x512 YUV420; no 1920x1080 worst case.
- yres_virtual defaults to two screens; DT mode 1 takes line_length from
  xres; fb0 gets the DT rotation in var, overlays are set up unrotated.
- pan_display always re-applies the new offset (the public source left a
  dangling "if (...) //return 0;" guarding the var copy) and skips overlay 1
  while userspace has no overlay disabled (overlay_disable_required, set by
  the overlay enable/disable ioctl).
- no blanket overlay manager apply at probe; no printk in set_par (called
  on every GPU flip).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/video/owl/fb/owlfb-ioctl.c |   3 +
 drivers/video/owl/fb/owlfb-main.c  | 100 +++++++++++++++--------------
 drivers/video/owl/fb/owlfb-sysfs.c |   6 +-
 drivers/video/owl/fb/owlfb.h       |  14 ++--
 4 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 54 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/owl/fb/owlfb-ioctl.c b/drivers/video/owl/fb/owlfb-ioctl.c
